NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000007 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000008 "=encoding utf8"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000009 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000010 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000011 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000012 "Menlo - A CPAN client"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000013 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000014 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000015 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000016 "Menlo is a backend for I<cpanm 2.0>, developed with the goal to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000017 "replace L<cpanm> internals with a set of modules that are more"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000018 "flexible, extensible and easier to use."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000019 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000020 "=head1 COMPATIBILITY"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000021 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 "Menlo is developed within L<cpanminus> git repository at C<Menlo>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 "subdirectory at L<https://github.com/miyagawa/cpanminus>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "Menlo::CLI::Compat started off as a copy of App::cpanminus::script,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 "but will go under a big refactoring to extract all the bits out of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "it. Hopefully the end result will be just a shim and translation layer"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 "to interpret command line options."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 "=head1 MOTIVATION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 "cpanm has been a popular choice of CPAN package installer for many"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "developers, because it is lightweight, fast, and requires no"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 "configuration in most environments."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 "Meanwhile, the way cpanm has been implemented (one God class, and all"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "modules are packaged in one script with fatpacker) makes it difficult"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "to extend, or modify the behaviors at a runtime, unless you decide to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "fork the code or monkeypatch its hidden backend class."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "cpanm also has no scriptable API or hook points, which means if you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 "want to write a tool that works with cpanm, you basically have to work"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "around its behavior by writing a shell wrapper, or parsing the output"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 "of its standard out or a build log file."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "Menlo will keep the best aspects of cpanm, which is dependencies free,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 "configuration free, lightweight and fast to install CPAN modules. At"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 "the same time, it's impelmented as a standard perl module, available"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 "on CPAN, and you can extend its behavior by either using its modular"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "interfaces, or writing plugins to hook into its behaviors."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "=head1 FAQ"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 "=item Dependencies free? I see many prerequisites in Menlo."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 "Menlo is a set of libraries and uses non-core CPAN modules as its"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 "dependencies. App-cpanminus distribution embeds Menlo and all of its"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 "runtime dependencies into a fatpacked binary, so that you can install"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 "App-cpanminus or Menlo without having any CPAN client to begin with."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 "=item Is Menlo a new name for cpanm?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 "Right now it's just a library name, but I'm comfortable calling this a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 "new package name for cpanm 2's backend."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000069 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000070 "=head1 AUTHOR"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000071 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000072 "Tatsuhiko Miyagawa E<lt>miyagawa@bulknews.netE<gt>"
